PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel has maintained a unanimous consensus on Choice F (Extension). The patient's immunocompromised profile combined with L4–S1 symptoms aggravated by lying supine strongly indicates an occult retroperitoneal process such as an iliopsoas abscess. Placing the patient in the left lateral decubitus position and performing passive hip extension stretches the iliopsoas muscle across the pelvic brim, reproducing the characteristic symptoms to elicit the psoas sign and confirm the diagnosis.
}

