18.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a unanimous consensus on Choice F (Extension). The clinical presentation of an immunocompromised patient with subacute L4–S1 pseudo-radicular pain aggravated by lying supine points to an occult retroperitoneal process, such as an iliopsoas abscess. In physical examination kinematics, following resisted active hip flexion while supine, passive hip extension performed in the contralateral lateral decubitus position stretches the iliopsoas across the pelvic brim to elicit the psoas sign and confirm the diagnosis. Competing musculoskeletal conditions such as piriformis syndrome and gluteal tendinopathy are excluded by postural and positioning mechanics. The standing directive is to maintain Choice F through the remaining rounds.
}

